      "description": "<p>Party’s economic spokesperson says donations are a ‘breakthrough moment’ as Labour’s Angela Rayner warns of possible retrospective action</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/13/reform-uk-donations-new-bill-retrospective-effect-angela-rayner\">Reform UK’s £72m donations may be caught by new bill, Rayner suggests</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/12/christopher-harborne-matches-36m-reform-donation-of-ben-zelo\">Christopher Harborne matches £36m Reform donation of Ben Delo</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/sep/12/reform-uk-billionaire-donations-analysis\">Analysis: Donations of £72m make Reform’s prospects both rosier and riskier</a></p></li></ul><p>Will also point out here that across the Sunday politics shows this morning, neither Labour nor the Tories ruled out accepting such huge sums from crypto-billionaires in the future.</p><p>Nigel Farage says that donations just go to putting Reform on a “more level playing field” with the more established parties.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/13/reform-uk-nigel-farage-robert-jenrick-christopher-harborne-ben-delo-donations-funding-anthropic-ai-uk-politics-latest-news-updates\">Continue reading...</a>",
