    {
      "title": "Only slim chance target of building 1.5m homes in England will be met, minister says",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/sep/13/slim-chance-government-target-building-homes",
      "description": "<p>Angela Rayner says manifesto pledge is not being dropped but focus is now on building council houses</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/politics/live/2026/sep/13/reform-uk-nigel-farage-robert-jenrick-christopher-harborne-ben-delo-donations-funding-anthropic-ai-uk-politics-latest-news-updates\">UK politics live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The government is unlikely to meet its target of building 1.5m homes in England, Angela Rayner has acknowledged, saying there was only a “slim chance” enough houses would be built before the next election.</p><p>The manifesto pledge to build 1.5m houses by the next election was a “stretch target”, the communities secretary added, but said it was not being ditched and she was “definitely not giving up”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/sep/13/slim-chance-government-target-building-homes\">Continue reading...</a>",
